# .dockerignore: what Docker must NOT send into the image (Phase 1, reviewed in Phase 18).
# Patterns start at the project folder; **/ means "in any folder".
# Smaller image, faster builds, and - most important - no secrets or personal files inside.

# --- Secrets and accounts: NEVER in an image (they arrive as environment variables) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data/users.json
data/accounts
.streamlit/secrets.toml
*.pem
*.key

# --- Version control, editors, local environments, caches ---
.git
.github
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.venv
venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
.idea
.vscode

# --- Generated at run time: these live on volumes, not in the image ---
data/*
!data/sample
models
vector_store
mlruns
logs
reports
**/*.db

# --- Not needed to run the app ---
tests
docs
notebooks
data_science
deployment
migrations
# (Dockerfile itself is NOT ignored: `minikube image build` must send it with the files - Phase 20)
compose.yaml
docker-compose*.yml
**/*.md
!documents/*.md
